contentSections.body:
The full shape:

```
if (painLevel > 7) {
  console.log("Flare day — log it and rest.");
} else {
  console.log("Manageable today.");
}
```

`if (...)` holds a condition that must evaluate to a boolean. If it's `true`, the first `{ }` block runs and the `else` block is skipped entirely. If it's `false`, the reverse happens. Exactly one of the two blocks ever runs for a given `if`/`else` pair — never both, never neither.

